# Project Configuration

Stack and versions: `AGENTS.md` § Stack and `package.json`. Path aliases (`@/` only, never `../../`): `AGENTS.md` § Critical rules.

## Tailwind v4 (CRITICAL)

**There is no `tailwind.config.ts`.** All config is in `src/index.css`.

- Dark mode via the `.dark` class (NOT `darkMode: 'class'` in a JS config — that file does not exist); animations via the `tw-animate-css` package (a CSS import, not a PostCSS plugin).
- `@tailwindcss/vite` handles compilation — do NOT add tailwindcss to PostCSS.
- A new colour token: add the HSL value to `:root` and `.dark`, map it in `@theme inline`.

## i18n

- Translations in `public/locales/{lng}/{ns}.json`; all four scaffolded namespaces are eager (`src/lib/i18n/constants.ts`); when to go lazy: `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` § i18n namespace strategy.
- Language detection: `localStorage` → browser → fallback `'en'`. In dev, translations hot-reload when `public/locales/` changes.
- No hardcoded user-visible strings — always `t('key')`.

## Accessibility

- Semantic HTML first (`<button>`, `<nav>`, `<main>` over `<div role="...">`); ARIA only where semantic HTML is insufficient.
- Loading states `role="status"` + `aria-live="polite"`; error states `role="alert"` + `aria-live="assertive"`.
- Every interactive element is keyboard-reachable. shadcn/ui components include accessibility by default — don't override without reason.

## UI Quality — avoid the AI aesthetic

AI-generated UI has recognizable tells. For any UI work reject the default in favour of the tokens in `src/index.css`:

- **Palette**: the brand is `--primary` (Google Blue). Never reach for the AI-default purple/indigo. Use the semantic tokens (`primary`, `secondary`, `muted`, `accent`, `destructive`) — no raw hex, no `bg-violet-500`. A new colour needs a token, not a one-off literal.
- **Gradients and shadows**: the theme defines none — keep surfaces flat, depth subtle. No decorative `bg-gradient-to-*`, no `shadow-2xl` cards; shadcn/ui new-york defaults are the ceiling unless a design specifies more.
- **Radius and spacing**: respect the scale — `--radius` drives `rounded-sm/md/lg`; vary radius by hierarchy rather than `rounded-2xl`/`rounded-full` everywhere. Use the Tailwind spacing scale; don't apply uniform oversized padding (`p-8`/`gap-12`) everywhere.
- **Layout and copy**: content-first and priority-driven over a generic template hero with a uniform card grid; the LCP-priority element comes first (`performance.mdc`). Realistic content via `t()` keys, never lorem-ipsum — real strings reveal real wrapping and overflow.
- **Dark mode**: every surface reads in both themes — never hardcode a light-only colour. Charts use `--chart-1`…`--chart-5`.
- **Baseline only**: prefer Baseline "Widely available" Web APIs; a "Newly available" one (e.g. `scheduler.yield()`) needs a fallback.

## Interaction & base-layer states (binding)

- **States must be PERCEPTIBLY DISTINCT, not merely present.** A hover / active / focus / selection colour must not resolve to about the element's own default or background colour. Seen in the wild: a base link colour equal to its `hover:` colour (only the cursor changes); a `::selection` built on a near-background token (invisible selection). Chrome and nav links default to a neutral (`text-muted-foreground`) so the `hover:text-primary` shift shows.
- **Compound states stay COHERENT.** When two states co-occur (focus+invalid, hover+selected, disabled+focus) the more urgent one owns the shared channel (an invalid field recolours its focus ring, `aria-invalid:focus-visible:ring-destructive`; disabled cancels hover). Check state PAIRS, not just singles.
- **Base-layer globals** (`::selection`, base links, `:focus-visible`) are built on `--primary` / `--ring`, never on a quiet near-background token (`--muted`, or an `--accent` that is a near-background neutral). For `::selection` use `background-color: hsl(var(--primary)); color: hsl(var(--primary-foreground));`.

## PWA — load-bearing config (CRITICAL — DO NOT TOUCH casually)

Several service-worker and manifest settings are **decided once / destructive to change**. NEVER change one without explicit approval (Approval Law). Reference and threat model: `.cursor/brain/PWA.md`; the reasoning for each: `.cursor/brain/SKELETONS.md`.

- **`registerType: 'prompt'` is decided ONCE** (`VitePWA(...)` in `vite.config.ts`). Flipping it to `'autoUpdate'` (or back) post-deploy leaks the toast contract into production caches and force-reloads tabs, destroying mid-session form state.
- **Ship BOTH `apple-mobile-web-app-capable` AND `mobile-web-app-capable`** in `index.html`. MDN flags the `apple-*` one as deprecated, but iOS Safari still breaks home-screen splash screens without it. NEVER "clean up" the apparent duplicate.
- **MSW × Workbox precache order is load-bearing**: `removeMswPlugin()` stays registered BEFORE `VitePWA(...)` in `vite.config.ts`, so `dist/mockServiceWorker.js` is deleted before the precache scan. Reordering ships MSW's worker as a dead precache entry (a 404 storm on every install). `scripts/check-pwa.mjs` fails the build on it — never bypass it.
- **Two service workers never coexist**: `public/mockServiceWorker.js` (MSW, DEV-only, gated by `import.meta.env.DEV` in `src/main.tsx`) and `dist/sw.js` (vite-plugin-pwa, PROD-only, `devOptions.enabled: false`). Do not enable PWA in dev or register MSW in prod.
